\emph{(L2) Sensitivity to the shaping weights.} We report a systematic
sensitivity analysis for the fuzzy weight $\lambda$ across
$\{0.10, 0.25, 0.50\}$ on CICIoT2023 in Section~\ref{sec:r3_1_lambda}
(Table~\ref{tab:lambda_ablation} and
Fig.~\ref{fig:lambda_sensitivity}). The main finding is that the MSR
varies by at most ${{CIC_MSR_SPAN_PP}}$ percentage points across the
tested range, which means the numbers reported elsewhere in the paper
are not an artefact of a particular $\lambda$. The link-reward weight
$\mu$ is fixed at $0.05$ in all experiments;
Proposition~\ref{prop:invariance} guarantees that the optimal policy
set is preserved for any non-negative $(\lambda, \mu)$, so the choice
of $\mu$ cannot change the set of converged policies, only the speed
of convergence. A full two-dimensional $(\lambda, \mu)$ sweep and a
$\lambda = 0$ (no-shaping) control condition are left to future work.
